                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4ab27458-4ed9-4e1a-a0d3-d27422137900",
                        "entry_id": "6bcd09d0-2f29-3d77-808b-6a4ca361c93b",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "degusted"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                        "entry_id": "6bcd09d0-2f29-3d77-808b-6a4ca361c93b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To taste carefully to fully appreciate something; to savour"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e2ed41f6-e4d1-4f28-ab96-729dba995871",
                                "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                                "text": "If wine is to withdraw its most poetic countenance, the sun of the white dinner-cloth, a deity to be invoked by two or three, all fervent, hushing their talk, degusting tenderly and storing reminiscences &emdash; for a bottle of good wine, like a good act, shines ever in the retrospect — if wine is to desert us, go thy ways, old Jack! Now we begin to have compunctions, and look back at the brave bottles squandered upon dinner-parties, where the guests drank grossly, discussing politics the while, and even the schoolboy \"took his whack,\" like liquorice water."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b077359-ec0f-4b13-b922-00ba0bd00c57",
                                "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                                "text": "The bread was passing stale the cheese a trifle hard the beer somewhat flat but the pair had never degusted a meal with more relish."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c421189-8040-4503-9adc-70db5f40fa7b",
                                "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                                "text": "I began to tell him all the tale of the demons, at which relation, first of all, he cried \"Pshaw!\"... But after he had degusted the matter a little he bade me repeat it all again from the beginning..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e59ac86-fe99-42f1-be15-f9a9ee9b582d",
                                "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                                "text": "He took the bottle filled up his glass half full and degusted it, *en connoisseur*, and said it is good but mine at home is better, it is older"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbb70fa6-dc49-484e-918d-177be6f18987",
                                "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                                "text": "as the bird soars once more, the observer may see it [the fish] being slowly degusted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5cb316e-23c1-41d0-91b9-0090c93e1741",
                                "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                                "text": "Sentiment, the inward working of emotion, does not issue in action, and so becomes mere sentimentality, to be lingered over, sipped, and degusted, for its own sake."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "97b652d3-d389-4214-b580-9436d41b4f01",
                                "sense_id": "78dc52a0-523d-3024-abfd-c440e4f39895",
                                "text": "This book is meant to help you along in your own quest for cheese, and I hope that you do taste the cheeses that you read about. By the time you finish this book you should have degusted a lot of wonderful cheese."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
